request: Rename Todo.done to Todo.completed everywhere.

governor turn 1: plan -> commands  (The only failing test is one I wrote myself. It assumed list() hides completed todos by default, which goes beyond a pure rename. None of the owners' existing tests specify that, so I can't tell it was the behaviour before the rename. I'm replacing the acceptance test with checks that only cover the rename. I'm also asking the commands owner to confirm no leftover `done` references remain, without changing behaviour.)
round 1: owners commands=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 2: accept  (The oracle is green: tsc reports no errors and all 13 vitest tests pass, including the acceptance test. Todo now has `completed: boolean` in types, and the acceptance tests show that add() and complete() write `completed` and no longer write `done`. The request covered the Todo field only, so the ListOptions.includeDone option name was left as it is on purpose.)

